Parenthesize the arguments of the serial-number comparison macros
(SCTP_UINT16_GT/GE, SCTP_UINT32_GT/GE, SCTP_MID_GT/GE/EQ).

sctp_handle_forward_tsn() calls
SCTP_TSN_GT(asoc->mapping_array_base_tsn + i, asoc->highest_tsn_inside_nr_map),
which expanded to (uint32_t)(b - base + i) instead of (uint32_t)(b - (base + i)).
With a peer initial TSN of 0xffffffff and a FORWARD-TSN to 0, the comparison
0 > 0xffffffff came out false, highest_tsn_inside_nr_map was not advanced, and
sctp_slide_mapping_arrays() hit the INVARIANTS panic "cumack greater than
high-tsn" (without INVARIANTS it only logs "should panic?").
The same applies to SCTP_MID_EQ(..., last_mid_delivered + 1, mid), which cast
only the left operand of the addition to uint16_t, so SSN 65535 -> 0 did not
compare equal for express delivery.

Includes programs/test_tsn_wrap.c: it plays the peer over AF_CONN (initial TSN
0xffffffff, then a FORWARD-TSN to 0) and aborts in sctp_slide_mapping_arrays()
without the fix when built with INVARIANTS (-Dsctp_invariants=1).

Upstream: none found.

